//// Front 12 step 4.3 — `@todo()` is a body that aborts when reached, not a
//// value. The function type-checks with its declared return type, the program
//// prints what came before, and dies at the call.
////
//// Measured at `85f883bd` (2026-09-20): `before` then an abort on all four
//// backends. beam dies for a different reason — `{undef, main:notReady/0}`: the
//// function whose whole body is `@todo()` is not emitted at all, so the abort is
//// the missing function's, not the builtin's. The observable pair (stdout, a
//// non-zero status) is the same, so the cell passes there; the defect is noted
//// here and reported, not asserted (no row owns it).

fn notReady() -> i32 { @todo(); }

pub fn main() {
    @print("before");
    @print(notReady());
}
